column2090:
Dec 20, 2019 09:14;712020:1c4de9a1-879b-434d-ac02-16ce22b36c58;{color:#1f4e79}*Problem Description:*{color}


{color:#1f4e79}Slot 0/3/CPU0 A9K-24X10GE-TR auto reload{color}




{color:#1f4e79}*Problem Analysis:*{color}


{color:#1f4e79}1.After checked the history logs, the A9K-24X10GE-TR is auto reload due to NP0 initialization failure.{color}


{color:#1f4e79}Then LC is reloaded by the prm_server_ty process to recover this issue.{color}


{color:#1f4e79}LC/0/3/CPU0:Nov 24 17:19:21.470 GMT: prm_server_ty[317]: %PLATFORM-NP-0-INIT_ERR : np_thread_channel_bringup  NP0 has failed to initialize.{color}


{color:#1f4e79}LC/0/3/CPU0:Nov 24 17:19:21.481 GMT: pfm_node_lc[304]: %PLATFORM-PFM-0-CARD_RESET_REQ : Card reset requested by: Process ID: 1929298 (prm_server_ty), Target node: 0/3/CPU0, CondID: 1027, Fault Reason: Persistent Initialization Failure.{color}




{color:#1f4e79}2.After reloading, NP is fully initialization and LC boot up again.{color}




{color:#1f4e79}3.for the NP init issue,it is a transient parity issue if card can boot up again and stable for over 48 hours.{color}


{color:#1f4e79}From the reboot history,this is the first time LC is reboot due to prm_server_ty process and NP init issue.{color}




{color:#1f4e79}*Action Plan:*{color}


{color:#1f4e79}1.Monitoring slot 0/3/CPU0 A9K-24X10GE-TR status. If NP is faulty again in 48 hours, then RMA is needed.{color}
======================================================

