column2091:
Sep 25, 2019 22:18;615b3e9cc5388b00696ca529;Dear [~accountid:637dc4d82acfad92d7b10432], the IPV4 address {color:#172b4d}63.218.236.1{color}/32 is available for the iperf test.
RP/0/RSP0/CPU0:var01.seo03#sh route 63.218.236.1
Wed Sep 25 13:44:48.599 GMT
Routing entry for 63.218.236.0/23
 
{color:#172b4d}Hi {color}[~accountid:615b54e3c7bea400692dc947]{color:#172b4d}, you can check the following tickets for more details.{color}
{color:#172b4d}https://jira.pccwglobal.com/browse/AS3491-986.{color}

https://jira.pccwglobal.com/browse/AS3491-936 
 
B{color:#172b4d}asically, the 1st thing to do is to find an unused IPV4 address to generate UDP traffic from an iperf server.{color}
S{color:#172b4d}ee the example below.{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}jmalpas@iperf01:~$ iperf -c 63.223.7.1 -u -b 20M -t 999{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}Before generating traffic, it is required to add a static route and remove policy-maps on each end of the IP backbone link during the iperf test.{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}It is also required to add redistribute static under router isis PCCW on one end.{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}Always remove the all added configuration on each side and create a new policy-map with the right usable bandwidth on the IP backbone link.{color}{color}
 
F{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}or cr01.hkg15:{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}RP/0/RSP0/CPU0:cr01.hkg15#sh run interface GigabitEthernet 0/0/0/14
Wed Sep 25 13:39:43.038 GMT
interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0/14
 description BACKBONE;;65004;HKG15;150Mb;22196-052019P;HKG15 - SEO03 [148M];HKG(PCG)-SEL(PCG) EP5612;Asia;;connect to VAR01.SEO03 Gi0/0/0/7 via SKBB+TX
 mtu 4782
 service-policy output core-queuing-148M  --> to be removed during the test.
 ipv4 address 63.218.236.62 255.255.255.252{color}{color}
 
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}router static{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}address-family ipv4 unicast{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}63.218.236.1/32 63.218.236.61 description test-IPEname -{color:#172b4d}-> to be added during the test.{color}{color}{color}
 
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}For var01.seo03:{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}RP/0/RSP0/CPU0:var01.seo03#sh run int gigabitEthernet 0/0/0/7
Wed Sep 25 13:39:48.254 GMT
interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0/7
 description BACKBONE;;65004;SEO03;150Mb;22196-052019P;HKG15 - SEO03 [148M];HKG(PCG)-SEL(PCG) EP5612;Asia;;connect to CR01.HKG15 Gi0/0/0/14 via SKBB+TX
 mtu 4782
 service-policy output core-queuing-148M{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}  --> to be removed during the test.{color}{color}
 ipv4 address 63.218.236.61 255.255.255.252
{color}{color}
 
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}router static{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color:#172b4d}address-family ipv4 unicast{color}{color}
{color:#172b4d}63.218.236.1/32 63.218.236.62 description test-IPEname --> to be added during the test.{color}
 
{color:#172b4d}router isis PCCW{color}
{color:#172b4d}address-family ipv4 unicast{color}
{color:#172b4d}redistribute static{color:#172b4d} --> to be added during the test.{color}{color}

