Oct 25, 2018 20:15;712020:2d2e2cb8-22ac-42e2-8d15-6b9e7bcf7072;[~accountid:637dc4d82acfad92d7b10432]

I do not thinking its safe to have an unpatched windows server running on the network for that long knowing fully well it is accessible form the internet. The vulnerability identified on this server is a critical one meaning there are a couple of exploits out there that could be targeted at it.

{color:#172b4d}Is there any compensating control we can put in place prior to when it is decommissioned? is there any reason we can't have it patched?{color}

column2100:
Apr 24, 2019 05:04;637dc4f1a593cb822e9419f7;The functionality of this server has been replicated on a new server.  Unfortunately the data being produced on it is being consumed by a server in HKG that has no maintenance.  Any updates to the server risk breaking the current data exchange.

There is a project underway to replace the functionality of the server in HKG.  Good contacts for that project would be Richard Danner.  
