column2093:
Jul 20, 2018 01:25;637dc4d82acfad92d7b10432;*+{color:#1f497d}IPE-1730 - Renaming Project from CR to BR{color}+*

 *+{color:#1f497d}{color}+* 

*+{color:#1f497d}Below is the revised list  of remaining CR routers to be renamed to AR/BR or VAR{color}+*{color:#1f497d}1.    {color}

{color:#1f497d}1.             cr04.lax04 -> br04.lax04{color}

{color:#1f497d}2.            cr03.sea01 -> br03.sea01 {color}

{color:#1f497d}3.            cr04.seo01 -> br04.seo01{color}

{color:#1f497d} {color}

{color:#1f497d} {color}

*+{color:#1f497d}Status update:{color}+* 

{color:#1f497d}1. Please rename the CR router to BR/VAR router in the respective Installation book. Contact Brian Tam to assist. {color}*{color:#c00000}Completed by Brian{color}*

{color:#1f497d}2. Please send email to DNS Admin to change the DNS forwards and DNS reverses from the CR router to the respective BR/VAR router. {color}*{color:#c00000}Completed by Roland & DNS team{color}* 

{color:#1f497d}3. Please send email to Engineering to rename all references of the CR router to BR/VAR router in ProvDB and relevant DB’s (Rancid, Prefix-list DB, etc). {color}*{color:#c00000}Will need to follow up with Engineering . I don’t see any response as of yet{color}* 

{color:#1f497d}4. Please send email to Steve and Wahyudi to change the ACS requests from CR router to BR/VAR router. {color}*{color:#c00000}ACS Updated by Steve Balon{color}*

{color:#1f497d}5. Please update Hostname in the router from CR to BR/VAR router. {color}*{color:#c00000}Will make the change when step 3 is completed{color}*

{color:#1f497d}6. Please update Interface Descriptions on either end to reflect router change from CR to BR/VAR.{color} *{color:#c00000}Will make the change when step 3 is completed{color}*

{color:#1f497d}7. Please open ticket with the underlying co-location provider to re-label the CR router to BR/VAR router for future reference.{color} *{color:#c00000}Will make the change when step 3 is completed{color}*

{color:#1f497d}8. Rename the routers on the MRV via the oobtelnet script on teton.. {color}*{color:#c00000}Will need to follow up with Cliff when step 3 is completed.{color}*

{color:#1f497d}9. Rename the customer names in ProvDB from the old CR to the new BR/VAR. {color}*{color:#c00000}Will need to follow up with Cliff{color}* 

{color:#376092}10. Shutdown any links between BR-VAR routers after the renaming has taken place{color}*{color:#c00000}. Will complete{color}*

{color:#1f497d}11. Check on the RR configuration as CR’s are IPv4 RR’s and after renaming to BR/VAR they become RR-clients.{color} *{color:#c00000}Will need to complete when steps 1 through 10 are completed{color}*
